he (feminine suffix)"}],"gloss":"wife"},{"surface":"தீரிய","parts":[{"text":"தீர்","lemma":"தீர்","gloss":"remove/end"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to remove"},{"surface":"இந்நிலை","parts":[{"text":"இந்நிலை","lemma":"இந்நிலை","gloss":"this state"}],"gloss":"this state","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"விடுத்தேன்","parts":[{"text":"விடு","lemma":"விடு","gloss":"leave/depart"},{"text":"த்த்","lemma":"த்த்","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"ஏன்","lemma":"ஏன்","gloss":"I (first person singular suffix)"}],"gloss":"I have departed"},{"surface":"வாழியர்","parts":[{"text":"வாழ்","lemma":"வாழ்","gloss":"live"},{"text":"இயர்","lemma":"இயர்","gloss":"optative suffix"}],"gloss":"may you live long"},{"surface":"குருசில்","parts":[{"text":"குருசில்","lemma":"குருசில்","gloss":"lord/patron"}],"gloss":"lord"},{"surface":"உதுக்காண்","parts":[{"text":"உது","lemma":"உது","gloss":"that over there"},{"text":"காண்","lemma":"காண்","gloss":"look"}],"gloss":"look there"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அவல","parts":[{"text":"அவல","lemma":"அவல","gloss":"sorrowful"}],"gloss":"sorrowful","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நெஞ்சமொடு","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சம்","lemma":"நெஞ்சம்","gloss":"heart"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"ஒடு","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with heart"},{"surface":"செல்வல்","parts":[{"text":"செல்","lemma":"செல்","gloss":"go"},{"text":"வல்","lemma":"வல்","gloss":"first person singular suffix"}],"gloss":"I will go"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"கறுத்தோர்","parts":[{"text":"கறு","lemma":"கறு","gloss":"hate/oppose"},{"text":"த்த்","lemma":"த்த்","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ஓர்","gloss":"those who"}],"gloss":"those who hated"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அருங்கடி","parts":[{"text":"அருங்கடி","lemma":"அருங்கடி","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"முனையரண்","parts":[{"text":"முனையரண்","lemma":"முனையரண்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"போலப்","parts":[{"text":"போலப்","lemma":"போலப்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருங்கை","parts":[{"text":"பெருங்கை","lemma":"பெருங்கை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யற்றஎன்","parts":[{"text":"யற்றஎன்","lemma":"யற்றஎன்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புலம்புமுந்","parts":[{"text":"புலம்புமுந்","lemma":"புலம்புமுந்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"துறத்தே","parts":[{"text":"துறத்தே","lemma":"துறத்தே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"Without considering your greatness in protecting mankind, / with a view devoid of righteousness, where love has vanished, / if people like you are also like this, / people like us will not be born here indeed! / My beloved wife of faultless principles, / if she has even a little life left in her, / it is difficult for her to remain without thinking of me; therefore, / saying, 'Has he become a stranger, so that the unrighteous god of death may mercilessly resolve to take my life?' / she who is in distress, grieving much and uttering words of sorrow, / to remove the suffering of that wife, from this state / I have departed. May you live long, Lord! Look there! / With a sorrowful heart, I will go. Those who hate you / like their heavily guarded frontier fortress, / my helplessness and grief are ahead of me!","translation":"Without considering your greatness in protecting mankind, if even people like you are devoid of righteousness and love, then people like us should never be born in this world! My beloved wife of faultless principles, if she still has a little life left in her, cannot live without thinking of me. Grieving deeply in her distress, she must be crying out, 'Has he become a stranger to me? May my life perish so that the merciless god of death can take it!' To relieve her of her suffering, I have now departed from this place. May you live long, O Lord! Look there! I go now with a sorrowful heart. Just like the heavily guarded frontier fortress of those who hate you, my helplessness and grief stand formidable before me!","modern":"மக்களைக் காக்கும் உன்னுடைய பெருமையை ஆராயாமல், அன்பு நீங்கிய அறமில்லாத தன்மையோடு உன்னைப் போன்ற கொடையாளர்களும் இப்படி நடந்து கொள்வார்களானால், எங்களைப் போன்ற இரவலர்கள் இனி இந்த உலகத்தில் பிறக்கவே மாட்டார்கள்! குற்றமற்ற கொள்கையுடைய என் அன்பான மனைவி, இன்னும் சிறிதளவு உயிர் பிழைத்திருப்பாளானால், என்னை நினைக்காமல் அவளால் இருக்க முடியாது. எனவே, 'அவர் எனக்கு அந்நியராகிவிட்டாரோ? என் உயிர் அழியட்டும், அறமற்ற எமன் என் உயிரைக் கொண்டு போகட்டும்' என்று கூறி, துன்புற்றுப் பலவாறு வருந்தி வாழும் என் மனைவியின் துயரத்தைத் தீர்ப்பதற்காக, நான் இந்த இடத்தை விட்டுப் புறப்பட்டுவிட்டேன். தலைவனே, நீ வாழ்க! அதோ பார், வருத்தமடைந்த நெஞ்சத்தோடு நான் செல்கிறேன். உன்னைப் பகைப்பவர்களுடைய அரிய காவல் பொருந்திய எல்லைக் கோட்டை போல, என் வறுமையும் தனிமையும் எனக்கு முன்னால் வந்து நிற்கின்றன!","explanation":"The poet Peruṅkuṉṟūr Kiḻār addresses the Cera king Ceramaṉ Kuṭakkōc Cēral Irumpoṟai in the theme of 'parisil kaṭānilai' (demanding gifts). Having waited long for the king's patronage without receiving any reward, the poet decides to leave in frustration. He laments that if even great kings like the Cera lack righteousness and love, then poor poets like him should not be born at all. He expresses deep concern for his devoted wife, who must be grieving in his absence, thinking he has abandoned her. The poet compares his overwhelming helplessness and grief to the formidable, heavily guarded frontier fortress of the king's enemies, illustrating his despair as he departs empty-handed.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}